msgid "The wallet starts checking the network from a starting point built into the program. It can make one of its own from the chain it has checked itself — a block well below the tip. From the next unlock the wallet starts from that point, so the start is shorter. Only you vouch for your own point: it is as good as the check this wallet has done. Money, keys and history are not touched."
msgstr "钱包从程序内置的一个起点开始检查网络,它可以从它自己检查过的链中创建一个自己的链 — — 远低于顶点的一个块。 从下一次解锁时开始,钱包从该点开始,所以开始时间更短。 只有你为自己的点担保:它与钱包所做的检查一样好。 钱、钥匙和历史记录不会被触及。"

msgid "The wallet starts checking the network from a starting point built into the program. It can make one of its own from the chain it has checked itself; from the next unlock it then starts from that one."
msgstr "钱包从程序内置的一个起点开始检查网络,它可以从它自己检查过的链中创建自己的链;从下一次解锁开始,它会从那个链开始。"

msgid "The wallet starts from the point built into the program, and the history before that point is proved by sampling its work. The wallet can make a point of its own further up, from the chain it has checked itself since then. From the next unlock it starts from there, so the start is shorter."
msgstr "钱包从程序内置的点开始,并通过采样其工作来证明该点之前的历史。 钱包可以从链中自我检查,从下一次解锁开始从那里开始,所以开始时间更短。"

